  "description": "tor before 0.4.9.9 was prone to a\u00a0NULL write after free when sending a CONFLUX_SWITCH cell fails. The return value of relay_send_command_from_edge() was   ignored, so a send failure (which calls circuit_mark_for_close()  and removes the leg via cfx_del_leg()) would go undetected, causing the caller to write to the now-freed current leg and resulting in a crash. This is TROVE-2026-017.",
